			<a name="custom0"></a><h3>Special Sessions</h3>
		<p>This conference is structured as a series of Special Sessions (see <a href="http://aca2009.etsmtl.ca/format.html" target="_self">Format</a> for more details). If you wish to organize a Special Session at ACA 2010, send your proposal to the Program Chairs. Be sure to include:  <ul type="circle"><li>the title of the Special Session,</li><li>the contact information of the organizers,</li><li>a short abstract stating the purpose of the Session.</li></ul> You should receive a quick response to your Session proposal once it has been evaluated by the Program Chairs (in collaboration with the ACAWG). Accepted Special Sessions are listed below. Organizers of Special Sessions are expected to maintain a website and are responsible for soliciting talks and contributions to their Session. (To submit an abstract, consult the link to the session that addresses your interests below.) Sessions are expected to contain at least 4 talks. The scientific quality of a Special Session is the sole responsibility of the session organizers. <p>Deadline for Session Proposals: May 15<sup>th</sup> 2010.</p></p>
		<div class="separator">&nbsp;</div>				<a name="custom1"></a><h3>Talks</h3>
		<p>All participants who would like to give talks must contact the chairs of the special sessions who are responsible for the scientific content of the sessions.<br />
<br />
You must register as an "author" in order to submit the abstract of the talk. Only talks submitted through the website will be accepted.</p>
